# emath-epic-machine-fjxh.9 negative seed.
#
# Scenario: a compiled semantic image whose partition payload is CORRUPTED
# (a flipped byte in the bytecode section, or a content id that no longer
# matches its partition) loads SILENTLY and executes wrong bytecode: a
# plausible distribution indistinguishable from the true cell formula.
# The image loader refuses typed instead: every partition carries a
# content id, the loader validates each partition independently, and a
# mismatch is a typed refusal — never a partial image, never a silent
# load.
#
# expect: E-IMAGE-001 - the loader refuses the corrupt partition with a
# typed refusal naming the partition; the image id never matches a
# corrupt build and partitions stay independently loadable.
use std.kinds.capability

emath capability Softmax:
    class: pure
    version: 1.0.0
    migration: frozen
    inputs:
        x: Vector[Float64]
    outputs:
        probability: Vector[Float64]
    image:
        # seeded corruption: bytecode page flipped after stamping
        partition: bytecode
        content_id: fnv1a64:0000000000000000
